<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Romanus (comes Africae)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 363–373</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Romanus was the Roman military count (comes Africae) of the African provinces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-i">Valentinian I</a>. When the Austuriani raided the countryside of Leptis and Oea in the 360s, he refused to act unless the cities supplied him with provisions and thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camels</a>, and later used his court connections to cover up the scandal. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ammianus-marcellinus">Ammianus Marcellinus</a> records his corruption, which also helped provoke the revolt of Firmus in Mauretania in the 370s.</p></div>
